 reading:{title:'Lunch at Cedar Café',text:'Cedar Café is a fictional practice restaurant. Its lunch menu is simple: chicken with rice costs $12, vegetable soup costs $6, and a bean sandwich costs $7. Still water costs $2 and orange juice costs $3. The listed prices are the full prices for this classroom role-play; there are no extra charges.\n\nRosa arrives at one o’clock. She asks for the menu. She wants soup, but the server says there is no soup today. Rosa chooses the chicken with rice instead. She orders still water because she does not want juice.\n\nAfter the meal, Rosa asks for the bill. The server brings it and Rosa checks the two items. She pays $14 and says thank you.',qa:[['Which food is unavailable?','Vegetable soup.','there is no soup today'],['What meal does Rosa choose?','Chicken with rice.','Rosa chooses the chicken with rice instead.'],['Why does she order water?','She does not want juice.','She orders still water because she does not want juice.'],['How much does she pay?','$14.','She pays $14 and says thank you.']]},
 listening:{title:'A Changed Order',script:'Welcome to Cedar Café. I am your server today. A customer named David sits at a small table by the window. He asks for the menu, and I give it to him. He looks at the food and drinks for a minute.\n\nDavid says he would like vegetable soup and a glass of orange juice. I explain that we do not have soup today. We have chicken with rice or a bean sandwich. David thinks for a moment. Then he says, I would like the bean sandwich, please. I repeat his order: one bean sandwich and one orange juice. He says that is right.\n\nI bring the juice first. A few minutes later, I bring the sandwich. David asks for a little more time before he pays. I say that is fine. After he finishes his meal, he asks for the bill. The sandwich is seven dollars, and the juice is three dollars. The total is ten dollars. There are no extra charges in this practice café. David checks the bill, pays ten dollars, and thanks me. I thank him too. He leaves the café and walks back to his class.',qa:[['What does David first want to eat?','Vegetable soup','he would like vegetable soup',['Vegetable soup','Chicken with rice','A bean sandwich']],['What drink does he order?','Orange juice','one bean sandwich and one orange juice',['Orange juice','Water','Coffee']],['What is the final total?','Ten dollars','The total is ten dollars.',['Ten dollars','Nine dollars','Fourteen dollars']]]},
 practiceA:[['Make this polite: Give me water.','Could I have some water, please?'],['You want chicken with rice. Place your order.','I would like the chicken with rice, please.'],['The soup is unavailable. Choose the bean sandwich.','I would like the bean sandwich instead, please.'],['Ask to see the list of dishes.','Can I see the menu, please?'],['Your meal is finished. Ask to pay.','Could I have the bill, please?']],
 practiceB:[['Ask whether the café has orange juice.','Do you have orange juice?'],['Order a bean sandwich and water.','I would like a bean sandwich and water, please.'],['You need another minute to choose. Tell the server.','Could I have another minute, please?'],['Confirm an order of chicken and juice.','Yes, chicken and orange juice. That is right.'],['The bill includes soup you did not receive. Explain politely.','Excuse me, I did not have soup. Could you check the bill, please?']],
